Primitive Variables vs Reference Variables:

Primitive Variables: These variables can only store one value at a time.
E.g. boolean, byte, char, double, float, int, long, short
Primitive instance variables can be initialized by java. However, it is recommended to initialize a value.

Reference Variables (References): Stores locations of objects in a memory. 
They usually refer to an object in the program. These objects contain instance variables and methods. 
E.g. String
By default, reference instance variables are null.
